    {
      "slide_number": 13,
      "slide_type": "content_two_column",
      "content": {
        "title": "Supervised vs Unsupervised Learning",
        "left_column": "SUPERVISED LEARNING:\n\n• Uses labeled data\n• Predicts specific outcomes\n• Examples:\n  - Classification\n  - Regression\n• Algorithms:\n  - Linear Regression\n  - Decision Trees\n  - Neural Networks\n• Use Cases:\n  - Spam detection\n  - Price prediction",
        "right_column": "UNSUPERVISED LEARNING:\n\n• Uses unlabeled data\n• Finds hidden patterns\n• Examples:\n  - Clustering\n  - Dimensionality reduction\n• Algorithms:\n  - K-Means\n  - PCA\n  - DBSCAN\n• Use Cases:\n  - Customer segmentation\n  - Anomaly detection"
      },
      "speaker_notes": "Both approaches have their strengths depending on your data and goals.",
      "transition": "fade",
      "duration": 40
    },
